# Warrant — example environment. Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# There is one variable, and most people will not need it. Snowflake credentials
# do NOT belong here: they live in ~/.snowflake/connections.toml and are read by
# `snow`, by `cortex`, and by the MCP server, so the agent inherits the operator's
# identity rather than holding one of its own.
#
# The database and warehouse are not configurable. They are spelled into the SQL
# as WARRANT and WARRANT_WH, because the stored procedures, the tag references and
# the grants all name them literally — a variable here would have implied an
# indirection that does not exist. tools/check_doc_claims.py now fails the build on
# any variable in this file that nothing reads, which is how the two of them, and a
# Slack webhook secret for a notification path that was never built, were found.

# Which connection in ~/.snowflake/connections.toml to use. Defaults to "warrant".
WARRANT_CONNECTION=warrant
